From 578f3e81f030272362d2b731869614f0affc2d77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:53:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Plugins: the player's place walked on from the last exact one

The client's movement to the server is encrypted, but its steps (a
31-byte segment about ten times a second) say whether the player moves.
Standing, the last exact place stays exact; walking, the place goes on at
the speed between the last two exact places (80 % of it, for up to 4 s of
moving), before the middle of what is around takes over again. The world
event says `moving`. Measured on a capture: 5.2 m off in the median
between exact reports before, 2.1 m now.
